{
  "dn10:0.1": "Long Discourses 10 ",
  "dn10:0.2": "With Subha ",
  "dn10:1.1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "dn10:1.1.2": "At one time Venerable Ānanda was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. It was not long after the Buddha had become fully quenched. ",
  "dn10:1.1.3": "Now at that time the student Subha, Todeyya’s son, was residing in Sāvatthī on some business. ",
  "dn10:1.2.1": "Then he addressed a certain young student, ",
  "dn10:1.2.2": "“Here, young student, go to the ascetic Ānanda and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Ask him if he is healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "dn10:1.2.3": "",
  "dn10:1.2.4": "And then say: ",
  "dn10:1.3.1": "‘Sir, please visit the student Subha, Todeyya’s son, at his home out of sympathy.’” ",
  "dn10:1.3.2": "“Yes, worthy sir,” replied the young student, and did as he was asked. ",
  "dn10:1.3.3": "",
  "dn10:1.3.4": "",
  "dn10:1.3.5": "",
  "dn10:1.3.6": "",
  "dn10:1.4.1": "When he had spoken, Venerable Ānanda said to him, ",
  "dn10:1.4.2": "“It’s not the right time, young student. ",
  "dn10:1.4.3": "I have drunk a dose of medicine today. ",
  "dn10:1.4.4": "But hopefully tomorrow I’ll get a chance to visit him.” ",
  "dn10:1.4.5": "“Yes, worthy sir,” replied the young student. He went back to Subha, and told him what had happened, adding, ",
  "dn10:1.4.6": "",
  "dn10:1.4.7": "",
  "dn10:1.4.8": "",
  "dn10:1.4.9": "",
  "dn10:1.4.10": "",
